.IX Title "ouse 3pm"
.TH ouse 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
ouse \- syntactic sugar to make Mouse one\-liners easier
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&  # create a Mouse class on the fly ...
\&  perl \-Mouse=Foo \-e \*(Aqhas bar => ( is=>q[ro], default => q[baz] ); print Foo\->new\->bar\*(Aq # prints baz
\&
\&  # loads an existing class (Mouse or non\-Mouse)
\&  # and re\-"opens" the package definition to make
\&  # debugging/introspection easier
\&  perl \-Mouse=+My::Class \-e \*(Aqprint join ", " => _\|_PACKAGE_\|_\->meta\->get_method_list\*(Aq
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fIouse.pm\fR is a simple source filter that adds \f(CW\*(C`package $name; use Mouse;\*(C'\fR
to the beginning of your script and was entirely created because typing
perl \f(CW\*(C`\-e\*(Aqpackage Foo; use Mouse; ...\*(Aq\*(C'\fR was annoying me... especially after
getting used to having \f(CW\*(C`\-Moose\*(C'\fR for Moose.
.SH INTERFACE
.IX Header "INTERFACE"
\&\f(CW\*(C`ouse\*(C'\fR provides exactly one method and it is automatically called by perl:
.ie n .IP """oose\->import()"">" 4
.el .IP \f(CWoose\->import()\fR> 4
.IX Item "oose->import()>"
Pass a package name to import to be used by the source filter.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.IX Header "DEPENDENCIES"
You will need Filter::Simple and eventually Mouse
.SH INCOMPATIBILITIES
.IX Header "INCOMPATIBILITIES"
None reported. But it is a source filter and might have issues there.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
oose for \f(CW\*(C`perl \-Moose \-e \*(Aq...\*(Aq\*(C'\fR
